    {
      "id": "claim_fa365a6d78bb422f877ccfacdecfc391",
      "statement": "When the server broadcasts a PeerDisconnectedMessage, the client fires the ZeroHubDisconnected status change and then tears the peer down through the shared removePeer helper, which clears the peer's pending ICE and P2P-recovery timers, closes the peer RTCPeerConnection, nulls its connection and ICE handlers, and removes the peer from the peers map.",
